TDD RED evidence for T-002 (tests/component-path-diff-basis.tests.sh),
captured post-hoc during quality-gate remediation
(reports/quality-gate/20260809T074500Z-epic-191-a3-path-ownership-T-002.md
Critical finding: implementation, tests, and GREEN logs landed together in a
single commit `ef151bdd`, with no RED commit anywhere in this feature's
history for this suite).

Methodology: rather than fabricate a RED log by editing a GREEN one, this
captures GENUINE red runs against `resolve-component-paths.py` with one
fail-closed check deliberately removed at a time -- reproducing, for real,
the state this suite would have observed before each corresponding
fail-closed clause existed. Each of the 5 named fail-closed axes
(unresolvable rev, invalid UTF-8, rename-limit-exceeded, TOCTOU,
submodule/symlink reference-only) is isolated in its own run against an
otherwise-correct implementation, then reverted before the next run, so each
run's failure is attributable to exactly one removed check and not to
interaction between multiple simultaneous defects. `git diff --stat` was
confirmed empty (implementation byte-identical to the real, correct,
currently-shipping code) both before this sequence started and after each
individual revert -- the product code that ships is untouched by this
evidence-capture process.

Every run below is the REAL suite (tests/component-path-diff-basis.tests.sh)
executed against the REAL CLI dispatcher (resolve-component-paths.sh ->
resolve-component-paths.py on this host), not a hand-edited transcript.
Axes 3 and 4 abort partway through the suite: their corresponding assertions
(TEST-023.2, TEST-025.2) are direct unit tests invoked without an `if`
guard in the suite script, so under `set -euo pipefail` a non-zero exit from
that direct invocation terminates the whole script immediately -- this is
itself genuine, reproducible behavior of the suite as authored, not an
artifact of this capture process.

