Note: the failure surfaces as a WRONG diagnostic ("no merge-base ...") from
the downstream compute_merge_base() check rather than as a clean success --
this is the genuine, honest consequence of removing only the
"unresolvable rev" fail-closed check while leaving the sibling
"no merge-base" check intact: the bogus rev's oid resolves to an empty
string instead of raising, which then fails a *different* fail-closed check
with the *wrong* message, exactly the kind of undiagnosable failure the
removed check exists to prevent. TEST-019.2 correctly identifies this as a
regression (grep for "unresolvable rev" does not match).

Reverted after this run; confirmed via `git diff --stat` (empty) and a
follow-up green run (17 passed, 0 failed) before starting axis 2.

