The suite aborts here (`set -euo pipefail`): TEST-023.2's python3 unit-test
invocation is not wrapped in an `if` guard in the suite script, so its
non-zero exit terminates the whole run immediately after printing this
"FAIL" line, before the suite's own `ok "TEST-023.2: ..."` /
`fail "TEST-023.2: ..."` wrapper or the final Results summary ever execute.
This is genuine behavior of the suite as authored (confirmed unchanged by
this remediation), not truncation by this capture process -- it is itself
proof the axis's own regression is caught, just via an abrupt script exit
rather than a tallied FAIL line.

Reverted after this run; confirmed via `git diff --stat` (empty) and a
follow-up green run (17 passed, 0 failed) before starting axis 4.

