unit-test invocation is unguarded, so `set -e` terminates the run
immediately after this FAIL line. Genuine: with the retry loop removed,
collect_changed_paths() never calls the monkeypatched
`_capture_fingerprint` at all, so the always-different fingerprint the test
injects is never observed and no exception is raised -- exactly the silent
"return a mixed-snapshot result instead of failing closed" defect this axis
exists to prevent.

